summary: 'Built the Classroom MVP as far as is safe autonomously, on branch classroom-mvp (4 commits: f55b25e6 wave1, b6adbc72 wave2a, e73d4ab6 wave2b, dacfab97 wave2c). The model is functionally end-to-end: (wave 1) the failure→reinforcement loop turns — a field break is attributed via orchestrationId, the learning is revised down, its cert overturned; (2a) the .syllabus artifact + scenario bank + field-failure→scenario converter + 6 MCP tools (paradigm_syllabus_*/scenario_*/classroom_status); (2b) repeat-failure-rate computed in ONE canonical place (premise-core/classroom-metrics.ts), surfaced in paradigm doctor; (2c) DRAFT skills /paradigm:class (gated certifier) + /paradigm:study-hall (autonomous stager), tool-verified, marked pending founder UX review. Verification caught real bugs each wave (missing reducer import that would''ve made the loop never run in prod; per-invocation dedupe defect) — green build was never trusted as proof. Final state: all 3 packages build; paradigm-mcp 489 tests + premise-core 42 tests green; reindex clean (1245 symbols, 0 lossy). NOT pushed (feature branch; Matt''s call to merge). Deferred per spec: the refinement engine (''X except Y'' Phase 2), more break signals + cross-domain read, decay pass, poison-pill standing control + peer-catch-rate (Phase 3), then University content (T-2026-06-19-003) + nevr.land (T-2026-06-19-004).'
